At the end of the show, the power goes out.

For a second, Brandon can hear the sound tech clicking the thunder button in the dark.

Then the kid in the front row stomps once.

The man at the back stomps twice. A woman halfway down the aisle starts drumming on her folding chair. It goes raggedly across the room until the whole place sounds like a storm coming up the street.

Brandon raises his hand out of habit. Nobody can see him. He lets it fall and stomps along.

The lights come back. The kid looks up at him, out of breath.

“Did we do it right?”

“I don’t know,” Brandon says. “Do it again.”